    Surface id-less case documents instead of dropping them silently
    
    Review of 7bae81c noted that a dict case lacking an id was now silently omitted
    from the index and report, where it previously failed loudly. Extract one
    _case_documents() helper used by both paths: non-case JSON (an evidence list,
    an empty placeholder) is skipped, but a non-empty dict without an id is named
    on stderr so a malformed real obligation stays visible while the pass
    continues. Regression asserts the warning and that it is not indexed.

